<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#guild">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Guild</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A guild is an association of craftsmen or merchants practising the same trade, organised to regulate production, training and standards and to protect members' interests. Guilds and comparable occupational corporations appear in many societies. The profiles note them in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gupta-empire">Gupta Empire</a>, in the craft organisation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin Empire</a>, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/songhai-empire">Songhai Empire</a> and in the economy of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akkadian-empire">Akkadian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/guild.jpg" alt="Guild" width="320" height="216" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rembrandt · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rembrandt_-_De_Staalmeesters-_het_college_van_staalmeesters_(waardijns)_van_het_Amsterdamse_lakenbereidersgilde_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
